---
import SystemOverviewLayout from "../../layouts/SystemOverviewLayout.astro";
import Button from "../../components/Button.astro";
---
<SystemOverviewLayout
  title="Courage"
  hook="Start in Slack. End with something you can inspect."
  description="Our private company assistant brings agent-assisted work to the place colleagues already talk. One example: turning a request into a working development preview."
  ogImage="/og/systems-courage.png"
>
  <Fragment slot="actions">
    <Button href="#preview-workflow">Follow a preview ↓</Button>
    <Button href="/systems/dev-center" variant="secondary">The tool underneath →</Button>
  </Fragment>
  <figure slot="visual" class="workflow-map">
    <figcaption class="label-caps">A preview request / Illustrated, not a real conversation</figcaption>
    <ol>
      <li><span class="step-symbol" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><span class="code-text-sm">SLACK</span><strong>“Can I try this change?”</strong><p>A colleague asks Courage.</p></div></li>
      <li class="tool-step"><span class="step-symbol" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><span class="code-text-sm">COURAGE + DEV CENTER</span><strong>A stack for the change.</strong><p>Worktree → services → development data</p></div></li>
      <li><span class="step-symbol" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><span class="code-text-sm">BACK TO THE COLLEAGUE</span><strong>Open it. Try it. Give feedback.</strong><p>A company-authenticated preview.</p></div></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="map-boundary"><span aria-hidden="true">↳</span> Development preview ≠ production release</div>
  </figure>

  <section class="system-section" id="preview-workflow">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <div><span class="eyebrow label-caps">Beyond a chat response</span><h2>“It works” is not the thing you need to review.</h2></div>
      <p>A running preview gives colleagues something to check for themselves. Here’s the workflow described in our public Dev Center case study.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="three-up">
      <article class="field-card"><span class="card-number">01 / ASK</span><h3>Begin where the work is discussed.</h3><p>Start the request in Slack. Colleagues don’t need to learn an engineering terminal workflow to ask for a preview.</p></article>
      <article class="field-card"><span class="card-number">02 / BUILD</span><h3>Reuse the engineers’ tool.</h3><p>Courage drives Dev Center through its CLI on its own machine. It prepares a stack rather than inventing a separate way to start the application.</p></article>
      <article class="field-card"><span class="card-number">03 / INSPECT</span><h3>Check the application, not the claim.</h3><p>Open the preview after company sign-in. It uses development data. A useful preview is not a production deployment or proof that a change is ready to ship.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="system-section shared-engine">
    <div><span class="eyebrow label-caps">The engineering choice</span><h2>One tool underneath. Different ways in.</h2><p>Dev Center runs locally, headlessly for Courage, and inside Crafting. The app and CLI share state and actions: we don’t maintain a separate stack launcher just for the agent.</p><a class="text-link" href="/systems/dev-center">See the app and CLI working together →</a></div>
    <div class="engine-diagram" aria-label="Engineers use the app and Courage uses the CLI; both use Dev Center">
      <div class="engine-inputs"><span>Engineers<br /><strong>Native app</strong></span><span>Courage<br /><strong>CLI</strong></span></div>
      <div class="engine-connector" aria-hidden="true">↓ <span>↓</span></div>
      <div class="engine-core">Dev Center<small>Same services · Same logs · Same state</small></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <aside class="reading-note">
    <div><span class="eyebrow label-caps">Used across Diversio. Kept private.</span><h2>The workflow is public.<br />The workplace isn’t.</h2><p>This is one example of Courage’s work—not a product launch, an access portal or a tour of internal conversations.</p></div>
    <div><p>For the technical story, read <a class="text-link" href="https://ashwch.com/all-tools-should-now-have-two-users.html">All tools should now have two users ↗</a></p><p class="small-note">Looking for tools you can use? Our open skills and extensions live in <a href="/agentic-tools">Agentic Tools</a>. They don’t grant access to Courage or our internal environments.</p></div>
  </aside>
</SystemOverviewLayout>
<style>
  .workflow-map { padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--color-surface); border: var(--border-hairline); border-radius: .75rem; box-shadow: 0 18px 48px rgba(35,16,82,.07); }
  figcaption { font-size: .65rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); line-height: 1.6; }
  ol { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
  li { display: flex; gap: 1rem; padding: 1.25rem; position: relative; background: var(--color-surface-low); border: var(--border-hairline); border-radius: .5rem; }
  li + li { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  li + li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1.5rem; background: var(--color-primary); left: 2.25rem; top: calc(-1.5rem - 1px); }
  .step-symbol { color: var(--color-primary); font-family: var(--font-code); font-size: .8rem; padding-top: .15rem; }
  li .code-text-sm { color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: .65rem; letter-spacing: .06em; }
  li strong { display: block; font-family: var(--font-headline); font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.3; margin: .5rem 0; }
  li p { color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: .8rem; }
  .tool-step { background: var(--color-primary-container); border-color: var(--color-primary); }
  .map-boundary { border-top: var(--border-hairline); padding-top: 1rem; font-size: .75rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .map-boundary span { color: var(--color-primary); padding-right: .5rem; }
  .shared-engine { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; align-items: center; gap: 4rem; }
  .shared-engine h2 { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .engine-diagram { text-align: center; padding: 2rem; background: var(--color-surface-low); border-radius: .75rem; }
  .engine-inputs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem; }
  .engine-inputs span { border: var(--border-hairline); background: var(--color-surface); border-radius: .5rem; padding: 1rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: .8rem; }
  .engine-inputs strong { font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--color-text); }
  .engine-connector { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; color: var(--color-primary); padding: .5rem; font-size: 1.5rem; }
  .engine-core { background: var(--color-primary); color: white; border-radius: .5rem; padding: 1.5rem 1rem; font-family: var(--font-headline); font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .engine-core small { display: block; font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 400; margin-top: .5rem; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { .shared-engine { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2rem; } .workflow-map, .engine-diagram { padding: 1rem; } li { padding: 1rem; } }
</style>
